  <title>How Hack The Flag Works: Playing a CTF Over SSH</title>
</head>
<body>

<main class="guide">
  <a href="/" class="bracket guide-back">Hack The Flag</a>

  <h1>How it works</h1>
  <p>
    Hack The Flag runs in your terminal. There is no website to log in to and no
    client to install. You connect with SSH and everything happens there.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Connect</h2>
  <pre><code>ssh app.hacktheflag.net</code></pre>
  <p>
    There is no sign-up form and no password. The server identifies you by your SSH
    public key. The first time you connect it creates a player for that key and gives
    you a nickname. Every later connection from the same key is the same player.
  </p>
  <p>
    That means you need an SSH key. If <code>ls ~/.ssh/*.pub</code> shows nothing,
    create one first:
  </p>
  <pre><code>ssh-keygen -t ed25519</code></pre>
  <p>
    It also means your key is your account. Connect from another machine with a
    different key and you start from zero, so copy your key if you want to play
    from two computers.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Pick a riddle</h2>
  <p>
    The main menu has three places to go: Riddles, Scoreboard and My Progress. Move
    with the arrow keys, open with Enter, go back with Esc, quit with <code>q</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Riddles lists every challenge with its difficulty and whether you have solved it.
    Open one to read it. Each riddle is a cipher or a puzzle that leads to one answer.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Submit the answer</h2>
  <p>
    Type your answer into the riddle screen and press Enter. You are told straight
    away whether it is right. Capital letters do not matter. Wrong answers cost
    nothing, but submissions are rate limited, so guessing in bulk will not work.
  </p>
  <p>Flags look like this:</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;HTF-this_is_a_flag/&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>4. Scoring</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Difficulty</th><th>Points</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Easy</td><td>100</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Medium</td><td>200</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hard</td><td>300</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The first player to solve a riddle gets one extra point, which is what separates
    players who are otherwise level. Only solves made before the edition closes count
    toward the scoreboard.
  </p>

  <h2>New to this?</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://blog.hacktheflag.net/">blog</a> has guides on the tools and
    ciphers you are likely to meet.
  </p>
</main>

